==Trivia==
*Ultimate Way Big is the last [[Ultimate Forms|Ultimate Form]] introduced in '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]'''.
*Ultimate Way Big was hinted on the DVD cover of ''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: The Ultimate Ending]]'', where his back is shown, with him facing [[Ultimate Vilgax]].
*Before Ultimate Way Big was designed, [[Dwayne McDuffie]] stated he would love a design that is faithful to Way Big's '''[[wikipedia:Ultraman|Ultraman]]'''-ish roots, but fancier. He suggested using one of [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]]'s discarded alternate designs for him, and that if it was not possible, they could simply recolor regular Way Big's red into "Ben 10 green".{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/0/08/The_Ultimate_Enemy_Part_2_DRAFT-2.pdf ''The Ultimate Enemy: Part 2'' Script Second Draft]|group = script}}
*If [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]] were to be given the opportunity to redesign Ultimate Way Big, he would make him look similar to his [[Way Big (Classic)|regular form]]'s appearance in the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' but with extra eyes.{{Refn|[[:File:TP Ult. Way Big Concept.png]]|group = TNP}}
*If [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] were to redesign Ultimate Way Big, he wouldn't look anything like the [[Way Bad]]s.{{Refn|[[:File:How Derrick would had designed Ultimate Way Big.png]]|group = DJW}} Instead, he would had amped up his armor and take inspiration from other Ultraman heroes to make him look more upgraded.{{Refn|[[:File:How Derrick would had designed Ultimate Way Big2.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Ultimate Way Big's design and powers bears a striking resemblance to [[w:c:ultra:Ultraman Taro (character)|Ultraman Taro]] from the '''Ultraman''' franchise. His color scheme, however, bears more of a resemblance to [https://ultra.fandom.com/wiki/Ultraman_Dyna_(character) Ultraman Dyna].
**Ultimate Way Big leaping into the air with his right fist extended upwards is a reference to the "Rise" transformation used in the '''Ultraman''' franchise.
**Ultimate Way Big's body spinning and cosmic disk powers are references to Ultraman's High Spin and Ultra-Slash techniques respectively.

